-- DebtFree Native: atomic native snapshot restore preparation.
-- STATUS: NOT APPLIED; intentionally fail-closed preparation only.
--
-- T-058-B2 blocker: the installed schema has no canonical, owner-scoped server
-- snapshot reader or durable restore receipt protocol. A restore RPC cannot
-- safely compare one exact baseline across auth.users metadata (settings CAS),
-- debt revisions/tombstones, ledger rows, bills, and reconciliation anchors
-- without first defining and verifying that shared canonical projection.
-- The existing settings RPC strips debts from metadata and increments its CAS
-- revision; the debt RPCs require one expected row version per change; and the
-- ledger RPCs apply deltas. Treating those independent calls as a snapshot
-- restore would be non-atomic and could double-apply ledger history.
--
-- This file deliberately defines no function, table, grant, or mutation. It is
-- a guard against accidentally treating an incomplete migration as a feature.
-- Before replacing this guard with executable SQL, add and review a single
-- authenticated protocol that:
--   * derives auth.uid() in SQL, validates caller ownership and currency, and
--     never authorizes through raw_user_meta_data;
--   * locks/compares a canonical baseline covering every restored domain and
--     settings revision, then commits the complete snapshot in one transaction;
--   * revision-updates existing debts, refuses tombstoned identity revival,
--     and deletes omitted rows only for explicitly confirmed replacement;
--   * stores an owner + stable operation ID + canonical payload fingerprint
--     receipt in that same transaction and returns authoritative readback;
--   * validates all references/allocations and writes final debt balances once
--     without replaying historical transaction deltas;
--   * revokes PUBLIC/anon execution and grants only authenticated callers.
--
-- The application service remains disabled until that protocol is implemented,
-- applied to an isolated environment, and verified. Do not apply this file.
DO $$
BEGIN
  RAISE EXCEPTION 'NATIVE_RESTORE_UNAVAILABLE: canonical atomic snapshot and receipt protocol is not prepared';
END;
$$;
